\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Lemma}
\title{The trace total in each class}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For left multiplication on the rational Hurwitz fiber,
##{\trace_F L_z=4\operatorname{Re}z.}
For each class counted in \ref{fdip-00ZK},
##{\sum_{(U,V)\text{ with }(s,t)}\trace_F L_U
=c_{s,t}(4-s).}}

\proof{
\p{In the rational basis #{(1,\qi,\qj,\qk)}, left
multiplication by each of #{\qi,\qj,\qk} has zero
diagonal: it sends every basis element to a signed
different basis element. The scalar part of #{z} acts
as #{\operatorname{Re}z} on each of the 4 basis
vectors. Linearity of trace gives the first identity;
trace is unchanged by passage to the Hurwitz basis.}

\p{Swapping #{U} and #{V} preserves #{s} and negates
#{ab-ba}, so preserves #{t} as well. The two class
sums of #{\trace_F L_U} and #{\trace_F L_V} are
therefore equal. By \ref{fdip-00ZI}, at each pair
##{\trace_F L_U+\trace_F L_V
=4(\operatorname{Re}U+\operatorname{Re}V)=2(4-s).}
Sum and divide by #{2} in #{\mathbb Q} to obtain the
class total.}
}

\p{The left-multiplication trace component is
\leanref/tauceti{QuaternionAlgebra.trace_mulLeft},
specialized to ordinary quaternions. The finite class
sum also uses the swap of the two loop links.}
